WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.062 --> 00:00:15.283
looked at the Dragon King and sighed.

2
00:00:16.724 --> 00:00:18.025
right," said the monkey.

3
00:00:18.045 --> 00:00:20.626
"I did make a promise to Guanyin."

4
00:00:21.687 --> 00:00:23.728
He put down his teacup and stood up.

5
00:00:25.689 --> 00:00:26.229
you, my friend.

6
00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:27.910
I will visit again soon."

7
00:00:29.371 --> 00:00:30.792
Dragon King smiled.

8
00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:32.445
"Good luck, Wukong."

9
00:00:33.525 --> 00:00:36.087
The monkey hurried out of the Dragon King's palace.

10
00:00:40.909 --> 00:00:43.831
He found the Tang Monk traveling alongside a stream.

11
00:00:43.851 --> 00:00:47.253
"Master, I have returned," he called.

12
00:00:51.035 --> 00:00:52.776
glad you're back, Wukong," said the monk.

13
00:00:52.796 --> 00:00:55.637
"I'm hungry."

14
00:00:55.657 --> 00:00:59.980
"I'll find a village and beg for some food for you," said the monkey.

15
00:01:01.396 --> 00:01:03.138
"You don't need to do that," said the monk.

16
00:01:04.699 --> 00:01:05.500
rice in the bag.

17
00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:06.480
You can cook that."

18
00:01:07.781 --> 00:01:09.363
monk got down from the horse.

19
00:01:13.806 --> 00:01:15.047
Wukong opened the bag.

20
00:01:16.528 --> 00:01:19.271
he looked inside, his eyes opened wide.

21
00:01:20.291 --> 00:01:21.853
He pulled out the headband.

22
00:01:23.874 --> 00:01:25.556
"This headband is marvelous!"

23
00:01:25.916 --> 00:01:26.676
said Wukong.

24
00:01:28.358 --> 00:01:30.800
said the monk, watching the monkey closely.

25
00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:31.881
"Do you like it?"

26
00:01:31.961 --> 00:01:34.362
"Yes!" said Wukong.

27
00:01:34.382 --> 00:01:36.744
"Try it on," said the monk.

28
00:01:36.764 --> 00:01:39.887
"Really?" asked Wukong.

29
00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:41.788
The monk nodded.

30
00:01:43.709 --> 00:01:44.790
put the headband on.

31
00:01:49.734 --> 00:01:51.775
He looked at his reflection in the stream.

32
00:01:51.835 --> 00:01:54.137
"I look handsome!"

33
00:01:54.437 --> 00:01:55.198
said Wukong.

34
00:01:55.218 --> 00:01:58.528
"Thanks for—ahh!"

35
00:01:58.548 --> 00:02:01.170
The monkey grabbed the sides of his head and fell over.

36
00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:03.431
eyes bulged.

37
00:02:03.451 --> 00:02:06.392
"My head's going to explode!"

38
00:02:06.713 --> 00:02:07.273
he cried.

39
00:02:09.214 --> 00:02:11.655
He saw the Tang Monk talking quietly.

40
00:02:11.675 --> 00:02:14.957
"Wh What are you saying?"

41
00:02:15.217 --> 00:02:16.038
cried Wukong.

42
00:02:17.098 --> 00:02:19.840
The Tang Monk stopped talking, and the pain stopped.

43
00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:24.262
"The bodhisattva Guanyin taught me a spell," said the monk.

44
00:02:25.383 --> 00:02:27.484
"She gave me the headband to force you to be good."

45
00:02:29.124 --> 00:02:30.285
pulled at the headband.

46
00:02:30.885 --> 00:02:32.126
But it wouldn't come off.

47
00:02:33.306 --> 00:02:35.047
stuck!" cried the monkey.

48
00:02:35.847 --> 00:02:37.048
He stamped his foot.

49
00:02:37.068 --> 00:02:38.568
"You tricked me!"

50
00:02:40.249 --> 00:02:41.910
for your own good," said the monk.

51
00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:44.091
"You must stop being violent."

52
00:02:45.532 --> 00:02:49.273
Wukong pulled out his iron bar and lunged at the Tang Monk.

53
00:02:52.655 --> 00:02:55.256
The monk recited the Tight Headband spell again.

54
00:02:56.708 --> 00:03:00.290
Wukong fell to the ground and rolled around in pain.

55
00:03:02.311 --> 00:03:03.112
"It hurts!

56
00:03:03.212 --> 00:03:04.192
It hurts!"

57
00:03:04.552 --> 00:03:05.133
he cried.

58
00:03:05.153 --> 00:03:07.114
"Please stop!

59
00:03:07.314 --> 00:03:08.955
I won't try to hurt you again!"

60
00:03:08.975 --> 00:03:13.537
The Tang Monk stopped, and the monkey stood up.

61
00:03:13.557 --> 00:03:17.179
"Now will you cook some rice?"

62
00:03:17.559 --> 00:03:18.120
asked the monk.

63
00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:21.922
"I'll get a fire started," said Wukong.

64
00:03:23.042 --> 00:03:25.904
The monkey waited until the Tang Monk had turned his back.

65
00:03:27.044 --> 00:03:29.146
Again he raised the iron bar.

66
00:03:30.166 --> 00:03:32.388
But the Tang Monk saw Wukong's shadow.

67
00:03:32.408 --> 00:03:38.052
"Ahh!" cried Wukong, once again falling to the ground.

68
00:03:38.833 --> 00:03:41.775
The Tang Monk looked furious as he recited the spell.

69
00:03:42.796 --> 00:03:44.317
Wukong's head pounded.

70
00:03:44.337 --> 00:03:46.558
"Please stop!"

71
00:03:46.939 --> 00:03:47.719
cried the monkey.

72
00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:51.062
The Tang Monk stopped reciting the spell.

73
00:03:51.082 --> 00:03:54.044
"Don't try to hit me again," said the monk.

74
00:03:54.816 --> 00:03:58.219
"If you do, I'll recite the spell until your head really does explode."

75
00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:01.522
sorry, Master," said Wukong.

76
00:04:01.542 --> 00:04:02.843
"I'll be good!"

77
00:04:06.265 --> 00:04:08.187
two traveled for a few more weeks.

78
00:04:10.088 --> 00:04:11.790
They arrived at a wide river.

79
00:04:12.971 --> 00:04:14.212
"How will we cross this river?"

80
00:04:14.552 --> 00:04:15.132
asked the monk.

81
00:04:15.152 --> 00:04:18.735
"It's too bad you're not a spirit," said Wukong.

82
00:04:20.176 --> 00:04:21.257
can leap over this river.

83
00:04:21.698 --> 00:04:22.799
But I can't take you with me."

84
00:04:23.999 --> 00:04:24.400
"Why not?"

85
00:04:24.744 --> 00:04:25.685
asked the Tang Monk.

86
00:04:25.705 --> 00:04:28.667
"You're a human," said the monkey.

87
00:04:28.687 --> 00:04:31.669
"So you must make the journey all by yourself.

88
00:04:32.709 --> 00:04:33.730
can only protect you.

89
00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:34.911
I can't carry you."

90
00:04:35.832 --> 00:04:36.892
"What will we do then?"

91
00:04:37.292 --> 00:04:37.913
asked the monk.

92
00:04:38.673 --> 00:04:43.216
Before Wukong could answer, the water swelled and a dragon leaped from it.

93
00:04:47.659 --> 00:04:48.120
"Look out!"

94
00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:49.100
cried the monkey.

95
00:04:51.082 --> 00:04:54.264
He yanked the Tang Monk off the horse as the dragon struck.

96
00:04:55.552 --> 00:05:01.018
With one bite, the dragon swallowed the horse and then slipped back underwater.
